HUD — visual design

Display exactly three small horizontal bars.

Order from left to right:

Pink | Yellow | Cyan

They should be visually separate bars with a small consistent gap between them.

Each bar represents two hits.

Each bar should visibly support exactly these states:

* full
* half
* empty

A full bar displays 100% colored fill.

A half bar displays 50% colored fill.

An empty bar keeps its subtle dark track/frame visible but has no colored fill.

Do not replace the bars with:

* hearts
* shield icons
* circles
* numbers only
* six tiny pips
* one large health bar
* a radial meter

They must remain three distinct bars.

A subtle midpoint divider may be used so the two-hit structure is easy to understand at a glance.

Keep the design minimal.

Use Seren’s existing:

* dark glass surfaces
* thin hairlines
* compact geometry
* restrained effects
* small radii
* peripheral HUD placement

Do not add large labels such as SHIELD over the road unless necessary for accessibility markup rather than visible presentation.

